## Formal Memory Lifecycle Authority

The stable lifecycle CLI is:

`~/.local/share/agent-memory-beacon/runtime/.venv/bin/python ~/.local/share/agent-memory-beacon/runtime/scripts/memory_lifecycle.py`

- Search and preview first with `list --id <memory-id> --json` or `list --query <text> --json`. Use the exact ID and current revision returned by that preview.
- Run `supersede`, `retract`, `expire`, `restore`, or `schedule-expiry` with `--expected-revision` and `--apply` only after an explicit user instruction authorizes that exact formal-memory transition.
- Apply a complete old-memory approval plan only through `memory_lifecycle_batch.py`, and only when the user explicitly authorizes that plan's exact Canonical SHA256; preview remains read-only without `--apply`.
- An inferred conflict, repeated correction, or apparently obsolete memory is not mutation authority. Route it through `propose`; proposals stay under `04-Feedback/_lifecycle-proposals/` and cannot enter recall.
- Automatic mutation is limited to `sweep-expired --apply`, and only records with an existing, already-passed `expires_at` are eligible.
- Formal memory and its evidence history must not physically delete. Inactive records stay auditable, and learners must not reactivate them.
- Claude Code and ZCode are collection-only for this lifecycle contract; they must not apply formal-memory transitions.

