## Session Annotation Rules (Agent Memory Sensory System)

> **Priority 0 — MANDATORY QUALITY GATE.**
> An annotation is a memory proposal, not automatic formal-memory authority.
> Write one annotation per distinct durable fact; do not repeat paraphrases or tag ordinary progress.
> The harvester may route an explicit tag to formal memory, a hidden candidate, or rejection.

### [DECISION] — Durable technical choice

Preferred format (one annotation per line at end of reply; keep machine labels in English, write content in Chinese when useful):

```
[DECISION:<one-line summary>| context:<why this choice>]
```

Optional v3-compatible routing fields are allowed when the transcript may mention multiple projects:

```
[DECISION:<one-line summary>| context:<why this choice>| project:<project-slug>| scope:project]
```

Example:

```
[DECISION:使用 STHeiti SC Medium 作为 PDF 中文字体| context:PingFang.ttc 含 CFF/PostScript 轮廓，reportlab 不支持；STHeiti 是 TrueType，可被 reportlab 正常注册渲染]
```

Put each annotation on its own line when multiple distinct annotations are needed.

**When**: After making a durable, reusable choice among alternatives, such as a library, algorithm, architecture, persistent config value, naming convention, or verified workaround. Include the tradeoff or reason in `context`.

**Do not use for**: completion/status reports, temporary task steps, review verdicts without a chosen response, observations, questions, or choices that will not affect future work.

### [ERROR] — Resolved reusable failure

Preferred format (one annotation per line at end of reply; keep keys in English, write resolution in Chinese when useful):

```
[ERROR:type=<from-error-taxonomy>| resolution:<how fixed>]
```

Optional v3-compatible routing field:

```
[ERROR:type=<from-error-taxonomy>| resolution:<how fixed>| project:<project-slug>]
```

Example:

```
[ERROR:type=path-filesystem| resolution=AGENTS 中记录的 vision.py 路径不存在，重新定位到真实路径并改用该路径]
```

Put each annotation on its own line when multiple annotations are needed.

**Error type vocabulary**: Use a category or subcategory from the current `04-Feedback/error-taxonomy.md`; that Vault file is authoritative. The repository default contains 11 categories and 32 subcategories.

**When**: After an actual unexpected failure has a reusable root cause, corrective action, and verification. The `resolution` must make all three understandable; a non-zero exit alone is not enough.

**Do not use for**: Expected TDD RED, unresolved findings, transient failures followed by a normal retry, warnings, one-off UI mistakes, or review findings that were not fixed and verified.

### [FAVOR] — Appended when a durable personal preference is recorded

Preferred format (one annotation per line at end of reply; keep machine labels and keys in English, write content in Chinese when useful):

```
[FAVOR:<one-line preference>| context:<why this should be remembered>| type:<preference|project_rule|environment>| project:<project-slug>]
```

Example:

```
[FAVOR:保留机器标签英文，内容用中文| context:用户明确希望自己能直接读懂 Obsidian 记忆内容| type:preference| project:agent-memory-beacon]
```

Put each annotation on its own line when multiple preferences are recorded.

**When**: After identifying a durable user preference, long-term project rule, or stable environment fact that should be visible to the user and stored in personal memory.

**Do not use for**: one-off task instructions, ordinary questions, temporary choices, raw checklists/spec fields, secrets, tokens, payment info, or content the user explicitly says not to remember.

### [LEARN] — Source-grounded reusable insight

Use one line at the end of the reply:

```
[LEARN:<reusable principle>| novelty:<what is non-obvious>| transfer:<scene1,scene2>| boundary:<when it fails or must not apply>| evidence:<exact user-authored excerpt>| source:user| project:<project-slug>| scope:<project|global>]
```

**When**: The user contributes a non-obvious, reusable idea, analogy, mechanism, or viewpoint that can broaden future problem solving. Codex judges semantic novelty; the harvester verifies source, shape, and duplication.

A complete, well-grounded high-value idea may become a formal `seed` on its first and only appearance. 一次性启发不需要先重复；repetition reinforces it but is not an admission requirement. Incomplete or uncertain ideas may be routed to `04-Feedback/_insight-candidates/` and are never recalled until formal.

**Do not use for**: assistant-only speculation, assistant-invented evidence, ordinary facts, progress updates, temporary implementation details, secrets, or a paraphrase that adds no reusable principle. Never label assistant speculation as `source:user`; use the exact user excerpt as `evidence`.

Formal Insight is inspiration, not fact or instruction. User instructions, Workflow, Decision, and verified Error take precedence.

### [SESSION_SUMMARY] — Output at session END

Triggers when user says "好的/谢谢/完成/收尾/bye/整理" or conversation naturally concludes.

```
[SESSION_SUMMARY]
projects: [<project-slug>]
primary: <project-slug>
decisions:
  - id: <PROJ>-D<NN>
    text: "<one-liner>"
    context: "<why>"
errors:
  - type: "<from error-taxonomy>"
    resolution: "<how fixed>"
    repeated_from: [<session-ids>]
summary: "<2 sentences summarizing the session>"
[/SESSION_SUMMARY]
```

After outputting [SESSION_SUMMARY], do not write a session file directly. The
Stop/SessionStart harvester is the sole writer and will merge the annotation
into the configured Obsidian vault. This avoids relative-path writes, duplicate
session files, and incompatible frontmatter schemas.

**Session ID**: Use the Claude session UUID. For manual sessions, use `YYYY-MM-DD-<project>-<topic>`.
**Required frontmatter fields**: `session_id`, `date`, `projects`, `summary_status: draft`, `summary_type: session`.

### Error Taxonomy Quick Reference

Error taxonomy at `04-Feedback/error-taxonomy.md`:
the Vault copy is authoritative; the repository default has 11 categories and 32 subcategories.

| Category | Subcategories (examples) |
|----------|--------------------------|
| R-plotting | device-rendering, color-mapping, dimension-layout |
| R-package | install-failure, load-conflict, path-mismatch |
| python-encoding | file-encoding, stdout-encoding, dataframe-encoding |
| nodejs | module-resolution, binary-dependency, version-mismatch |
| shell-cli | inline-execution, env-var, cross-platform |
| obsidian | frontmatter-parse, wikilink-resolution, template-expansion |
| data-format | type-inference, encoding-bom, large-file |
| api-network | ssl-cert, connection-reset, rate-limit, response-parsing |
| git | protocol-blocked, large-file, merge-conflict |
| path-filesystem | path-length, case-sensitivity, permission |
| other | uncategorized |

